{"content":[{"c":["MICA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Common name interchangeable with Micah and probably a contracted form of Micaiah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Mephibosheth’s son. He shared in the fortunes of David’s generosity to his father, and in Ziba’s treachery (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.9.12","r":"2Sam.9.12","rawR":"2Sam.9.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.9.12","value":"2Sam.9.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 9:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-space","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Levite and Zicri’s son from Asaph’s clan (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.15","r":"1Chr.9.15","rawR":"1Chr.9.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.15","value":"1Chr.9.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:15"},"), who performed musical service in the temple. He appears to have been one of the exiled priests whose son Mattaniah was among the first group of returning exiles (also called “the son of Zabdi,” ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.17,22","r":"Neh.11.17,22","rawR":"Neh.11.17,22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.17,22","value":"Neh.11.17,22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:17, 22"},", and Micaiah, the son of Zaccur, ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.35","r":"Neh.12.35","rawR":"Neh.12.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.35","value":"Neh.12.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. One who set his seal on Ezra’s covenant during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.11","r":"Neh.10.11","rawR":"Neh.10.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.11","value":"Neh.10.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mica","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 9:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.9.12","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.9.12","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.9.12"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.15"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:17, 22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.17,22","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.17,22","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.17,22"},{"anchorText":"12:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.35","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.35","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.35"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.11","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.11","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3bfae25e2add688b85082b6020dcb54e612bfe26669bf05ffc0fcbdbf8ea26d4","sourceItemName":"Mica","sourceItemOrder":298,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Mica","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mica","title":"Mica","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}